^{:go/end 1831} (go/method AddInteriorSym "AddInteriorSym sets up 'interior' as an interior symbol of\ncontainer/payload symbol 'container'. An interior symbol does not\nitself have data, but gives a name to a subrange of the data in its\ncontainer symbol. The container itself may or may not have a name.\nThis method is intended primarily for use in the host object\nloaders, to capture the semantics of symbols and sections in an\nobject file. When reading a host object file, we'll typically\nencounter a static section symbol (ex: \".text\") containing content\nfor a collection of functions, then a series of ELF (or macho, etc)\nsymbol table entries each of which points into a sub-section\n(offset and length) of its corresponding container symbol. Within\nthe go linker we create a loader.Sym for the container (which is\nexpected to have the actual content/payload) and then a set of\ninterior loader.Sym's that point into a portion of the container.\n" [^{:tag (* Loader)} l ^Sym container ^Sym interior]
  ;; The interior symbols for a container are not expected to have
  ;; content/data or relocations.
  (when (!= (len (.Data l interior)) 0)
    (panic "unexpected non-empty interior symbol"))

  ;; Interior symbol is expected to be in the symbol table.
  (when (.AttrNotInSymbolTable l interior)
    (panic "interior symbol must be in symtab"))

  ;; Only a single level of containment is allowed.
  (when (!= (.OuterSym l container) 0)
    (panic "outer has outer itself"))

  ;; Interior sym should not already have a sibling.
  (when (!= (.SubSym l interior) 0)
    (panic "sub set for subsym"))

  ;; Interior sym should not already point at a container.
  (when (!= (.OuterSym l interior) 0)
    (panic "outer already set for subsym"))

  (aset (.-sub l) interior (aget (.-sub l) container))
  (aset (.-sub l) container interior)
  (aset (.-outer l) interior container))



